# Two shapes a doc comment cannot be written for. A language whose
# comment prefix has no marker in it leaves nothing to write with,
# and the driver does not refuse it, it dies partway with the file
# unwritten. A delimiter quoted at column zero inside an example body
# is an anchor to org's backward text search and is not one to a
# tree, so the two engines would disagree about where an extent
# begins and both would write a file.

# oracle: skip blank.org emacs dies partway here rather than
# refusing, and quoted.org is the divergence this refusal exists to
# prevent, so neither can be compared.

! exec babble tangle blank.org
stderr 'no comment marker'
! exists blank.out

! exec babble tangle quoted.org
stderr 'quoted at column zero'
! exists quoted.go

-- .lit/comments.json --
{"blank": " "}
-- blank.org --
#+title: a language with no marker

* Nothing to write with

The docstring that cannot be wrapped.

#+begin_src blank :tangle blank.out :comments org
whatever
#+end_src
-- quoted.org --
#+title: a delimiter quoted inside an example

* The paragraph org will not see

#+begin_example
#+end_src
#+end_example

#+begin_src go :tangle quoted.go :comments org
package quoted
#+end_src
